.TH CVEC_AT_PTR 3 "2026-08-15" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cvec_at_ptr \- access element at index (type-inferred, returns pointer or NULL)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

element_ptr = cvec_at_ptr(v, index);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This macro is a type-inferred wrapper for cvector_at(). It gives a pointer to
the element. It gives NULL when the index is out of bounds. The macro casts
to the correct type automatically. cvec_at stops the program for such an
index, but this macro does not.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
v      Vector to access
index  Zero-based index of the element
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Gives a pointer to the element at the index
Gives NULL when the index is out of bounds
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The macro gives NULL when the index is out of bounds. It does not stop
the program.
The pointer stays valid only until the size of the vector changes.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cvec_construct(vec, int);
cvec_push(vec, 42);
int *ptr = cvec_at_ptr(vec, 0);
if (ptr) {
  *ptr = 5; // Change the element in place
}
cvec_destroy(vec);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvector_at (3),
.BR cvec_at (3)
